/-!
# Reproducible builds and transformation integrity

This umbrella collects the dependency-minimal relational core and its
composition, certified-planning, two-sided-hosting, relational GSLT-IL, and
OSLF operational-correspondence bridges, together with source-scoped
trajectory replay and the theorem-backed Hatta R1--R5 profile.
Prime DAG replay and HE derivation-local state-free execution are retained as
separate instances of that boundary.
Recursive verifiability is proved only for current modifications carrying a
protected map of the complete R1--R5 certificate family.
Observer-indexed audit legibility is ordered by sufficient views and actual
permitted verification plans; hierarchical rank is an attained readout, not
an intrinsic property of a transformation or a proxy for attestation.
R7 verification plans retain exact checked occurrences, WorkSpan, and
retained-evidence storage; sampled, selective, and full coverage have distinct
conclusions, and resource feasibility remains independent of semantics and
current attestation.
Dynamic-link routes retain ordered, machine-readable provenance while
relational interoperability remains distinct from functional representation,
global ledger gluing, and external legal adjudication.
The R1--R7 coverage matrix contains actual positive and negative proof terms
and records each row's attribution and premise boundary.
-/
